<title>USA: Zero sees Q1 sales, EPS up over prior year.</title>
<headline>Zero sees Q1 sales, EPS up over prior year.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zero Corp said Wednesday it expects its first quarter earnings per share to increase by about 20 percent and for its sales to be up about 15 percent.</p>
<p>The company said it expects the 1998 fiscal year to post record results based on the strength of its backlog and the growing markets it serves.</p>
<p>Zero, which is primarily involved in protecting electronics, posted net income of $3.8 million, $0.31 per share, on sales of $54.66 million in the prior year's first quarter.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
